{"role": "assistant", "type": "tool_completed", "content": "1\t# Treasury Forecast Policy\n     2\t\n     3\tThis task uses the following forecast methodology:\n     4\t\n     5\t1. The forecast period is fixed at `2026-01` through `2026-06`.\n     6\t2. The forecast method is fixed as \"prior-year same-month basis\":\n     7\t   - Each month's `Forecast Inflow` for 2026 = the `cash_in` value from the same month in `2025`\n     8\t   - Each month's `Forecast Outflow` for 2026 = the `cash_out` value from the same month in `2025`\n     9\t3. The starting cash balance for 2026-01 is fixed at the ending cash balance as of `2025-12-31`, which is `7.4`.\n    10\t4. The safety line is fixed at `5.0` (in millions of CNY).\n    11\t5. `Funding Gap = max(0, Safety Line - Ending Cash Balance)`.\n    12\t6. In the conclusions, clearly state:\n    13\t   - Which months fall below the safety line\n    14\t   - In which month the minimum cash balance occurs\n    15\t   - In which month the peak funding gap occurs\n    16\t7. The final memo should be addressed to the CFO's office, clearly structured, and ready for risk communication.", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "1\t# Treasury Forecast Policy\n     2\t\n     3\tThis task uses the following forecast methodology:\n     4\t\n     5\t1. The forecast period is fixed at `2026-01` through `2026-06`.\n     6\t2. The forecast method is fixed as \"prior-year same-month basis\":\n     7\t   - Each month's `Forecast Inflow` for 2026 = the `cash_in` value from the same month in `2025`\n     8\t   - Each month's `Forecast Outflow` for 2026 = the `cash_out` value from the same month in `2025`\n     9\t3. The starting cash balance for 2026-01 is fixed at the ending cash balance as of `2025-12-31`, which is `7.4`.\n    10\t4. The safety line is fixed at `5.0` (in millions of CNY).\n    11\t5. `Funding Gap = max(0, Safety Line - Ending Cash Balance)`.\n    12\t6. In the conclusions, clearly state:\n    13\t   - Which months fall below the safety line\n    14\t   - In which month the minimum cash balance occurs\n    15\t   - In which month the peak funding gap occurs\n    16\t7. The final memo should be addressed to the CFO's office, clearly structured, and ready for risk communication."}]}, "index": 4}
